CAT = "dronAerodrome"; SEG = "AER"
Q = [
("Without meeting any extra conditions, how close to an aerodrome boundary may a drone fly?",
 "No closer than 4 km", ["No closer than 2 km", "No closer than 8 km", "No closer than 1 km"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3 sets the line at 4 km from the boundary of any aerodrome. Inside it the pilot needs a qualification or supervision and the aerodrome's authorisation or agreement."),
("From where is the 4 km aerodrome distance measured?",
 "The aerodrome boundary", ["The control tower", "The runway centreline", "The main terminal building"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3 says a person must not fly on or within 4 km from the boundary of an aerodrome without meeting its conditions."),
("Which pilot may fly an unshielded drone within 4 km of an aerodrome, if the other conditions are met?",
 "One with an approved qualification", ["One who has flown for a year", "One with a manufacturer's certificate", "One with a model club badge"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3 requires a pilot qualification issued by an approved person or organisation under rule 101.202, supervision by its holder or an appointed instructor, or a Part 61 or Part 149 licence or certificate."),
("A student pilot with no drone qualification wants to fly within 4 km of an aerodrome. Which arrangement allows it?",
 "Supervision by a qualified holder", ["An observer standing beside them", "Flying below 200 ft", "A spotter with a handheld radio"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3 allows a person under the direct supervision of the holder of an approved pilot qualification, or of an instructor appointed by an approved organisation."),
("Which aviation document also meets the pilot requirement for flying a drone near an aerodrome?",
 "A Part 61 pilot licence", ["A Part 47 certificate", "A Part 102 exposition", "A Part 139 aerodrome certificate"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(1)(iii) accepts the holder of a pilot licence or certificate issued under Part 61 or Part 149."),
("A qualified pilot wants to fly 3 km from a controlled aerodrome. What else is needed?",
 "Authorisation from ATC", ["The aerodrome cafe's consent", "A Part 102 certificate", "A NOTAM seven days ahead"],
 "For a controlled aerodrome, CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(2) requires the flight to be in accordance with an authorisation from the relevant ATC unit."),
("A qualified pilot wants to fly 2 km from an uncontrolled aerodrome. Whose agreement is needed?",
 "The aerodrome operator's", ["The nearest ATC unit's", "The local police station's", "The CAA Director's"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(3) says a flight within 4 km of an uncontrolled aerodrome must be done in accordance with an agreement with the aerodrome operator."),
("Near an uncontrolled aerodrome, what must each drone pilot have with them while the aircraft is airborne?",
 "An observer", ["A second drone", "A spare transmitter", "A radio licence"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(3)(iii) requires an observer in attendance for each pilot, giving extra situational awareness and alerting the pilot to approaching aircraft."),
("What is the observer's job when a drone flies near an uncontrolled aerodrome?",
 "Warn the pilot of other aircraft", ["Fly the drone if the pilot tires", "Phone the aerodrome each minute", "Hold the landing pad steady"],
 "CATI 101-1 says the observer provides extra situational awareness and alerts the pilot to any approaching aircraft."),
("Within 4 km of an uncontrolled aerodrome, how high may a drone fly without the Director's approval?",
 "400 ft above ground level", ["200 ft above ground level", "500 ft above ground level", "1,000 ft above ground level"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(3)(iii)(B) says the drone must not go higher than 400 feet above ground level unless the Director has approved the operator to fly higher."),
("Do the 4 km aerodrome rules apply to a hospital helipad?",
 "Yes, if it is in the AIPNZ", ["No, helipads are always exempt", "Only when a helicopter is visible", "Only at night"],
 "Part 101 counts any aerodrome promulgated in the AIPNZ, and the CAA's guidance tells drone pilots to stay 4 km from hospital and sightseeing helipads unless the requirements are met."),
("A free flight model glider is launched within 4 km of an uncontrolled aerodrome with the operator's agreement. Where must it be launched?",
 "Downwind of the active runway", ["Upwind of the active runway", "On the runway threshold", "Beside the aerodrome windsock"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(3)(ii) says a free flight model aircraft must be launched downwind of an active runway."),
("Does the pilot qualification requirement near aerodromes apply to free flight model aircraft?",
 "No, it does not", ["Yes, always", "Only for gliders", "Only near controlled aerodromes"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(c) says the pilot qualification paragraph does not apply to a free flight model aircraft. The aerodrome authorisation and agreement rules still do."),
("An uncontrolled aerodrome lies inside controlled airspace. What does a qualified drone pilot need there?",
 "Operator agreement and ATC", ["The operator's agreement only", "ATC approval only", "No approval if under 400 ft"],
 "AC101-1 notes that some uncontrolled aerodromes sit inside controlled airspace, so the pilot needs the aerodrome operator's agreement and an ATC authorisation for the airspace."),
("A pilot has ATC authorisation to fly 3 km from an airport. What does that authorisation cover?",
 "Only the airspace near it", ["Every other Part 101 rule", "Consent from people below", "Flying above 400 ft anywhere"],
 "AC101-1 says ATC authorisation only permits the flight within 4 km of the aerodrome boundary. It does not confirm compliance with any other Part 101 rule."),
("Why should a drone pilot give an aerodrome operator as much notice as possible?",
 "Late requests may be declined", ["It sets the flight's landing fee", "It registers the drone", "It removes the observer rule"],
 "AC101-1 advises giving as much notice as possible when seeking agreement from an aerodrome operator or ATC unit, otherwise permission to fly may be declined."),
("A pilot has no drone qualification and no supervisor. How close to an uncontrolled aerodrome may they fly unshielded?",
 "No closer than 4 km", ["No closer than 2 km", "Inside 4 km below 200 ft", "Anywhere outside the runway"],
 "AC101-1's table says a pilot with no licence, qualification or qualified supervisor must stay at least 4 km from the boundary of any aerodrome, controlled or uncontrolled."),
("A drone flies behind a row of tall buildings 2 km from an aerodrome. When can this skip the aerodrome rules?",
 "Shielded, under 33 ft above it", ["If it stays below 400 ft", "If an observer watches it", "If the aerodrome is uncontrolled"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(b) exempts a shielded flight outside the aerodrome boundary, no more than 33 feet above the shield, in airspace separated from the aerodrome by a barrier able to stop the aircraft."),
("For the shielded exception near an aerodrome, what must stand between the drone and the aerodrome?",
 "A barrier able to stop it", ["A painted line on the ground", "A sign saying no drones", "A person holding a red flag"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(b)(3) requires the airspace to be physically separated from the aerodrome by a barrier capable of arresting the flight of the aircraft, for example after a fly-away."),
("Can the shielded exception be used for a drone flown inside the aerodrome boundary?",
 "No, only outside it", ["Yes, if under 33 ft", "Yes, behind a hangar", "Yes, with an observer"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(b)(1) allows the shielded exception only for an operation conducted outside the boundary of the aerodrome."),
("Who can be approved to appoint drone instructors whose supervision counts near aerodromes?",
 "An approved organisation", ["Any aerodrome operator", "Any licensed drone retailer", "The local district council"],
 "Rule 101.202 lists appointing people to give instruction to RPA operators as one of the functions an approved person or organisation can perform; CATI 101-1 clause 2.3 accepts their supervision."),
("A qualified pilot has the aerodrome operator's agreement but no observer. May they fly 3 km from the uncontrolled aerodrome?",
 "No, an observer is needed", ["Yes, the agreement is enough", "Yes, if below 200 ft", "Yes, for under 10 minutes"],
 "At an uncontrolled aerodrome CATI 101-1 requires the operator's agreement and an observer for each pilot, plus the 400 ft limit. Every condition applies together."),
("Which place counts as an aerodrome for the 4 km rule even though it has no runway?",
 "A promulgated heliport", ["A school sports field", "A farm airstrip not in the AIP", "A beach car park"],
 "The rule turns on whether the aerodrome is promulgated in the AIPNZ. Heliports and helipads in the AIP count, while an unlisted private strip is not an aerodrome under Part 101."),
("A qualified pilot is 3 km from a controlled aerodrome but the drone will stay inside a large shielded area outside the boundary, behind a barrier and within 33 ft of the shield. What is needed?",
 "No aerodrome authorisation", ["ATC authorisation anyway", "An observer and an agreement", "A NOTAM 24 hours ahead"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(b) says paragraph (a), including the ATC authorisation and qualification, does not apply to a shielded operation that meets the boundary, height and barrier conditions."),
("Which statement about flying near aerodromes is correct?",
 "Controlled airspace goes past 4 km", ["Controlled airspace ends at 4 km", "Helipads have no 4 km zone", "Drones under 250 g are exempt"],
 "The CAA's airspace guide warns that controlled airspace around airports extends well beyond the 4 km limit, so ATC clearance can be needed even further out."),
("Where is the preferred place to look up aerodrome operator and ATC contact details before a flight near an aerodrome?",
 "The Airshare website", ["The aerodrome's car park", "A drone retailer's site", "The Part 47 register"],
 "AC101-1 says contact details for aerodrome operators and ATC units, and for other airspace, are available on Airshare."),
("A free flight model is to be flown 3 km from a controlled aerodrome. What is required?",
 "ATC authorisation", ["A drone pilot qualification", "Nothing, models are exempt", "Only an observer"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(2) needs ATC authorisation within 4 km of a controlled aerodrome for free flight models too. The pilot qualification paragraph does not apply to them."),
("Besides Part 61, a pilot licence or certificate issued under which rule part meets the pilot requirement near aerodromes?",
 "Part 149", ["Part 102", "Part 47", "Part 91"],
 "CATI 101-1 clause 2.3(a)(1)(iii) accepts a pilot licence or certificate issued under Part 61 or Part 149. Part 149 covers aviation recreation organisations that issue pilot certificates."),
]
